[length:03:20]
[ti:Grey eyes]
[ar:Aracne Phobia]
[al:Alignment: chaotic-dysfunctional]
[au:Aracne Phobia]
[lr:Aracne Phobia]
[by:Azaria]
[re:LRC Workbench by Azaria (lrc-workbench.azariadev.dev)]
[ve:0.2.7]
[00:01.55]She’s fine
[00:06.11]She’s always fine
[00:09.57]Look at her—
[00:11.82]big grey eyes, perfect smile
[00:18.29]She was the prodigy
[00:19.28]quiet and bright
[00:20.71]read all the endings
[00:21.73]before they were right
[00:23.09]Spoke to the pages
[00:24.25]more than to friends
[00:25.65]lived in the margins
[00:26.55]where silence extends
[00:28.24]Big grey eyes
[00:29.18]they shimmer, they lie
[00:30.48]she learned very early
[00:31.65]which parts to hide
[00:33.00]They say she’s lovely
[00:34.21]they say she’s rare
[00:35.61]no one gets close enough
[00:36.87]to see she’s aware
[00:38.96]She laughs on cue
[00:40.83]tilts her head just right
[00:43.50]she clocks every pattern
[00:45.63]but still plays it nice
[00:48.29]If she feels too much
[00:50.53]she renames the pain
[00:53.56]calls it “a phase”
[00:55.72]just to stay the same
[00:58.15]She smiles like nothing’s wrong
[01:01.71]like she belongs somewhere
[01:04.10]But she’s drifting through the room
[01:06.17]like nobody put her there
[01:09.09]Shining girl, don’t break the scene
[01:11.22]keep it soft, keep it clean
[01:13.72]She knows exactly what this is—
[01:16.10]but she can’t exit the machine
[01:18.83]♫
[01:23.06]She talks to cats
[01:24.16]like they understand
[01:25.62]they never ask her
[01:26.74]to become a plan
[01:28.14]She slows it down
[01:29.31]blurs out the sound
[01:30.48]needs something soft
[01:31.51]to not hit the ground
[01:33.98]Too much feeling
[01:35.05]under her skin
[01:36.17]she maps the damage
[01:37.47]but won’t give in
[01:39.00]She reads herself
[01:40.17]in every word
[01:41.18]but understanding
[01:42.54]just makes it worse
[01:44.16]They love her face
[01:45.70]they love her voice
[01:48.18]they love the version
[01:50.85]that makes less noise
[01:54.02]She feeds them lines
[01:56.03]she wrote alone
[01:58.36]a perfect mask
[02:00.79]that feels like home
[02:03.26]She smiles like nothing’s wrong
[02:06.74]like she’s already saved
[02:09.16]But she’s fading in plain sight
[02:11.03]like a role she learned to play
[02:14.03]Shining girl, don’t lose control
[02:16.51]keep the script, protect the role
[02:18.76]If she questions what she is
[02:20.94]there’s no one left to hold
[02:24.59]She says:
[02:26.50]“You don’t want to be like me”
[02:30.81]“I see it all before it hits
[02:32.87]I know exactly where this leads”
[02:35.50]“I built a cage that looks like grace
[02:40.11]and now I live inside the theme”
[02:44.37]“But if I drop it—
[02:45.77]there is nothing underneath”
[02:49.44]She’s fine
[02:53.37]She’s always fine
[02:56.77]Big grey eyes
[02:58.68]open wide
[03:00.51]She feels too much
[03:03.07]to ever stop
[03:05.48]So she just learns
[03:07.44]to call it life
[03:10.04]♫
